"char_end": 545,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s02"
},
{
"start": 210.0,
"end": 211.56,
"speaker_label": "Luc\u00eda Herrera",
"text": "I want to delve deeper into that.",
"char_start": 546,
"char_end": 579,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s03"
},
{
"start": 211.62,
"end": 215.22,
"speaker_label": "Luc\u00eda Herrera",
"text": "What's something you used to believe about this that you've since re-evaluated?",
"char_start": 580,
"char_end": 659,
"unit_id": "t0004.u01",
"sent_id": "t0004.s04"
},
{
"start": 215.22,
"end": 224.22,
"speaker_label": "Diego Ferrer",
"text": "It boils down to this: most mysterious creaking noises are resolved by cleaning the contact surfaces and re-tightening them to the specified torque.",
"char_start": 674,
"char_end": 822,
"unit_id": "t0005.u01",
"sent_id": "t0005.s01"
},
{
"start": 224.28,
"end": 227.28,
"speaker_label": "Diego Ferrer",
"text": "We've seen this happen with equipment that uses Spoke & Wrench.",
"char_start": 823,
"char_end": 886,
"unit_id": "t0005.u01",
"sent_id": "t0005.s02"
},
{
"start": 227.34,
"end": 231.12,
"speaker_label": "Diego Ferrer",
"text": "The frame matters because it tells you what compromises you're making.",
"char_start": 887,
"char_end": 957,
"unit_id": "t0005.u01",
"sent_id": "t0005.s03"
},
{
"start": 231.12,
"end": 232.38,
"speaker_label": "Luc\u00eda Herrera",
"text": "That's a useful framework.",
